   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Light Leak\n\nA warm analog light leak drifts across the frame, blows out at the cut and cools off on the next scene.\n\nCategory: transitions. Length: 0.6667 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- The video has a film, lifestyle or nostalgic look and the cut should feel like light hitting the negative.\n- A warm, soft cut between two scenes that would otherwise hard-cut, such as a montage of shots.\n- The palette should match a brand: the leak takes any colours.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The video is a crisp UI or data piece where a warm burn looks out of place: use fade-through.\n- The cut should feel like a camera move rather than light: use whip-pan.\n- Both scenes are very bright: the blow-out loses contrast.\n\nVariables:\n- origin (enum): Origin, default \"left\"\n- intensity (number, 0-1): Intensity, default 1\n- leak_color (color): Leak color, default \"#FF5A1F\"\n- blowout_color (color): Blow-out color, default \"#FFF3E0\"\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Light Leak\n\n  A warm analog light leak drifts across the frame, blows out at the cut and cools off on the next scene.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/light-leak/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"light-leak\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"0.6667\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"origin\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Origin\", \"description\": \"Edge the leak drifts in from.\", \"default\": \"left\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"left\", \"label\": \"Left\"}, {\"value\": \"right\", \"label\": \"Right\"}, {\"value\": \"top\", \"label\": \"Top\"}, {\"value\": \"bottom\", \"label\": \"Bottom\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"intensity\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Intensity\", \"description\": \"Strength of the leak and the blow-out, 0 to 1.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05},\n    {\"id\": \"leak_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Leak color\", \"description\": \"Color that leads the leak.\", \"default\": \"#FF5A1F\"},\n    {\"id\": \"blowout_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Blow-out color\", \"description\": \"Tint the frame blows out to at the cut.\", \"default\": \"#FFF3E0\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Light Leak</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@600&amp;display=block\" />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        #root { background: #0a0a0a; }\n        .ll-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        .ll-scene { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        .ll-panel { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; overflow: hidden; }\n        .ll-in { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 2.4cqmin; }\n        .ll-in span { font-family: Geist, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 9cqmin; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1; color: #f2f2f2; white-space: nowrap; }\n        .ll-bar { display: block; width: 14cqmin; height: 0.8cqmin; border-radius: 1cqmin; background: rgba(242, 242, 242, 0.55); }\n        .ll-pa { background: #141318; }\n        .ll-pb { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #3b3699 0%, #1e2a6b 55%, #0f4c75 100%); }\n        .ll-flare { position: absolute; inset: 0; mix-blend-mode: screen; opacity: 0; }\n        .ll-flash { position: absolute; inset: 0; opacity: 0; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"light-leak\" data-duration=\"0.6667\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"ll-clip\" class=\"ll-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"0.6667\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"ll-scene\" class=\"ll-scene\">\n            <div id=\"ll-a\" class=\"ll-panel ll-pa\"><div class=\"ll-in\"><span>Scene A</span><i class=\"ll-bar\"></i></div></div>\n            <div id=\"ll-b\" class=\"ll-panel ll-pb\"><div class=\"ll-in\"><span>Scene B</span><i class=\"ll-bar\"></i></div></div>\n          </div>\n          <div id=\"ll-flares\"></div>\n          <div id=\"ll-flash\" class=\"ll-flash\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return value !== \"\" && value !== null && Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, list, fallback) {\n              return list.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              return function (x) {\n                if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 32; i++) {\n                  var u = 1 - t;\n                  var cx = 3 * u * u * t * x1 + 3 * u * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                  if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                  t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                }\n                var v = 1 - t;\n                return 3 * v * v * t * y1 + 3 * v * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n              };\n            }\n            function clamp01(p) { return Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p)); }\n            function ip(x, a, b, from, to, ease) {\n              var p = b === a ? (x >= b ? 1 : 0) : clamp01((x - a) / (b - a));\n              return from + (to - from) * (ease ? ease(p) : p);\n            }\n            // Damped spring from 0 to 1, rest at 0 velocity (mass, stiffness, damping), at `frame` of 30 fps.\n            function spring(frame, cfg) {\n              if (frame <= 0) return 0;\n              var t = frame / 30, m = cfg.mass, k = cfg.stiffness, c = cfg.damping;\n              var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / m), z = c / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * m));\n              if (z < 1) {\n                var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n                return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + (z * w0 / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n              }\n              return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n            }\n            // Seeded generator (mulberry32).\n            function rng(seed) {\n              var a = seed >>> 0;\n              return function () {\n                a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n                var t = a;\n                t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n                t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n                return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n              };\n            }\n            var TOTAL = 0.6667;\n            var FRAMES = Math.round(TOTAL * 30);\n            var clock = { frame: 0 };\n            function frameNow() { return Math.round(clock.frame * 1000) / 1000; }\n            function start(draw) {\n              var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: FRAMES, duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(frameNow()); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"light-leak\"] = tl;\n            }\n            function onFonts(fn) {\n              if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) document.fonts.ready.then(fn, function () {});\n            }\n            function fit(el, size, frac, hfrac) {\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var maxW = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * frac);\n              var maxH = Math.max(1, root.clientHeight * (hfrac || 0.9));\n              var k = Math.min(1, maxW / Math.max(1, el.scrollWidth), maxH / Math.max(1, el.scrollHeight));\n              if (k < 1) { size = Math.max(8, size * k); el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; }\n              return size;\n            }\n\n\n            var origin = pick(vars.origin, [\"left\", \"right\", \"top\", \"bottom\"], \"left\");\n            var intensity = num(vars.intensity, 1, 0, 1);\n            var palette = [str(vars.leak_color, \"#FF5A1F\"), \"#E5322D\", \"#FFB347\", str(vars.blowout_color, \"#FFF3E0\")];\n            var blowout = palette[palette.length - 1];\n            var FLARES = [\n              { along: 0, across: 0.3, size: 0.85, alpha: 1 },\n              { along: -0.18, across: 0.78, size: 0.7, alpha: 0.85 },\n              { along: 0.12, across: 0.55, size: 0.55, alpha: 0.9 },\n              { along: -0.32, across: 0.12, size: 0.6, alpha: 0.7 },\n              { along: 0.05, across: 0.95, size: 0.5, alpha: 0.6 }\n            ];\n            var host = document.getElementById(\"ll-flares\");\n            var flareEls = FLARES.map(function (f, i) {\n              var d = document.createElement(\"div\");\n              d.id = \"ll-flare-\" + i; d.className = \"ll-flare\";\n              host.appendChild(d); return d;\n            });\n            var sceneEl = document.getElementById(\"ll-scene\"), flash = document.getElementById(\"ll-flash\");\n            var a = document.getElementById(\"ll-a\"), b = document.getElementById(\"ll-b\");\n            flash.style.background = blowout;\n            var driftE = bezier(0.3, 0.1, 0.5, 0.9);\n            function heat(p) {\n              if (p <= 0.5) { var q = p / 0.5; return q * q; }\n              var r = (p - 0.5) / 0.5; return 1 - (1 - (1 - r) * (1 - r));\n            }\n            var W = root.clientWidth, H = root.clientHeight, span = Math.max(W, H);\n            start(function (frame) {\n              var p = clamp01(frame / FRAMES);\n              var k = heat(p) * intensity;\n              // Hard cut under the blow-out: the incoming scene owns the frame from the midpoint.\n              a.style.visibility = p < 0.5 ? \"visible\" : \"hidden\";\n              b.style.visibility = p >= 0.5 ? \"visible\" : \"hidden\";\n              sceneEl.style.filter = \"brightness(\" + (1 + k * k * 1.6) + \") saturate(\" + (1 + k * 0.4) + \")\";\n              var drift = -0.25 + (1.05 + 0.25) * driftE(p);\n              var show = k > 0.001;\n              flareEls.forEach(function (el, i) {\n                var f = FLARES[i];\n                if (!show) { el.style.opacity = 0; return; }\n                var along = drift + f.along;\n                if (origin === \"right\" || origin === \"bottom\") along = 1 - along;\n                var horizontal = origin === \"left\" || origin === \"right\";\n                var x = (horizontal ? along : f.across) * W, y = (horizontal ? f.across : along) * H;\n                var color = palette[i % Math.max(1, palette.length - 1)];\n                el.style.opacity = Math.min(1, Math.sqrt(k) * f.alpha * 1.1);\n                el.style.background = \"radial-gradient(circle \" + (span * f.size) + \"px at \" + x + \"px \" + y + \"px, color-mix(in srgb, \" + color + \" 55%, \" + blowout + \") 0%, \" + color + \" 22%, color-mix(in srgb, \" + color + \" 55%, transparent) 45%, transparent 72%)\";\n              });\n              var fl = Math.exp(-Math.pow((p - 0.5) / 0.1, 2)) * intensity;\n              flash.style.opacity = show ? Math.min(0.96, fl) : 0;\n            });\n\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
